# ============================================================
# Ouriva — Reverse Proxy Template (Caddy)
# ============================================================
# Caddy terminates HTTPS (automatic Let's Encrypt certificates,
# no config needed) and forwards each subdomain to the matching
# container's published host port.
#
# One-time setup on the host:
#   1. Point DNS at the host: a wildcard record
#        *.ouriva.app  A  <host public IP>
#      (or one A record per subdomain if you'd rather not use
#      a wildcard) — plus ouriva.app itself if this host also
#      serves the main site.
#   2. Install Caddy: https://caddyserver.com/docs/install
#   3. Copy this file to /etc/caddy/Caddyfile and fill in the
#      real port numbers below.
#   4. sudo systemctl enable --now caddy
#
# After this file is in place at /etc/caddy/Caddyfile,
# provision-instance.sh appends a new block to it automatically
# for every instance it creates — you only need to hand-write
# the demo block below once.
# ============================================================

demo.ouriva.app {
    reverse_proxy localhost:3100
}

# provision-instance.sh appends one block like this per tester,
# right after this line — do not remove it, new blocks are
# inserted below.
